-- title:
--   Evaluating a symmetric form on basis vectors
-- statement:
--   A symmetric $j$-linear form $F$ on $K^r$ is given by coefficients $F(s)$ on multisets $s$ of size $j$, and evaluates as $F(v_1,\dots,v_j)=\sum_{a}F(\mathrm{sym}(a))\prod_iv_i(a_i)$ over all tuples $a:\{1..j\}\to\{1..r\}$, where $\mathrm{sym}(a)$ is the multiset of entries. For every tuple $a:\{1..j\}\to\{1..r\}$, with standard basis vectors $e_k$,
--   $$
--   F(e_{a_1},\dots,e_{a_j})=F(\mathrm{sym}(a)) .
--   $$
--
--   So the coefficients are exactly the basis values, and the coefficient description is faithful.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/MetricEntropy/SymmetricForms.lean#L66-L82

